# CVFairy — Core Project Rules

## Project Identity
- **Product:** CVFairy — AI-powered resume builder SaaS
- **Stack:** Next.js 16 (App Router) + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS 4 + shadcn/ui
- **Deployment:** Cloudflare Pages (free tier) with D1, R2, KV
- **Architecture:** Local-first (IndexedDB default, optional cloud sync)

## Agentic SDLC
Before implementing any feature, follow the agentic SDLC:
1. Read the task spec in `docs/knowledge-base/tasks/`
2. Verify the plan exists and dependencies are met
3. Implement step-by-step per the plan
4. Verify against acceptance criteria
5. Update knowledge base nodes
6. Commit with conventional commit message

## Absolute Rules
- TypeScript strict mode everywhere — no `any`, no `as` casts unless unavoidable (add comment explaining why)
- No `console.log` in committed code — use structured logging or remove
- No hardcoded secrets, API keys, or credentials — use environment variables
- No TODO/FIXME in shipped code — create a task node in `docs/knowledge-base/tasks/` instead
- Every function that can fail MUST handle errors explicitly (try/catch or Result type)
- Prefer early returns over nested conditionals
- Max function length: ~50 lines. Extract helpers if longer.
- Max file length: ~300 lines. Split into modules if longer.

## File Naming Conventions
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g., `ResumeEditor.tsx`)
- Hooks: `use-kebab-case.ts` (e.g., `use-resume-store.ts`)
- Utilities: `kebab-case.ts` (e.g., `pdf-export.ts`)
- Types/schemas: `kebab-case.ts` in a `types/` or `schemas/` directory
- Constants: `kebab-case.ts` (e.g., `template-defaults.ts`)
- Route files: follow Next.js conventions (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`)

## Import Order
1. React/Next.js imports
2. Third-party library imports
3. Internal aliases (`@/` prefix)
4. Relative imports
5. Type-only imports last

## Directory Structure
```
src/
  app/                    # Next.js App Router pages and layouts
    (marketing)/          # Marketing pages (landing, pricing, etc.)
    (app)/                # Authenticated app pages (editor, dashboard)
    api/                  # API route handlers
  components/
    ui/                   # shadcn/ui base components
    resume/               # Resume-specific components
    editor/               # Editor-specific components
    shared/               # Shared/layout components
  lib/                    # Core business logic
    schemas/              # Zod schemas (source of truth for types)
    stores/               # Zustand stores
    hooks/                # Custom React hooks
    utils/                # Pure utility functions
    ai/                   # AI integration (prompts, SDK config)
    export/               # PDF, DOCX, HTML export engines
    db/                   # Drizzle schema and queries
    auth/                 # Auth.js configuration
    stripe/               # Stripe integration
  templates/              # Resume template definitions
  i18n/                   # Internationalization messages
docs/
  knowledge-base/         # Obsidian-style knowledge graph
    tasks/                # Task specifications
    architecture/         # Architecture decision records
    requirements/         # Feature requirements
  sdlc/                   # SDLC methodology docs
  architecture/           # System architecture diagrams
```

## Environment Variables
- Prefix client-safe vars with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
- All secrets go in `.dev.vars` (Cloudflare local) or Cloudflare dashboard (production)
- Never commit `.dev.vars` or `.env.local`

## Git Conventions
- Branch naming: `feat/short-description`, `fix/short-description`, `chore/short-description`
- Commit format: conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `chore:`)
- Keep commits atomic — one logical change per commit

## Cloudflare Free Tier Limits (Stay Within These)
- D1: 5GB storage, 5M rows read/day, 100K rows written/day
- R2: 10GB storage, 1M Class A ops/month, 10M Class B ops/month
- KV: 100K reads/day, 1K writes/day, 1GB storage
- Workers: 100K requests/day, 10ms CPU time/invocation
- Pages: 500 builds/month, 1 build at a time
- Workers AI: 10K neurons/day
